ith a nearby word. A direct relation can still be a false assertion: keep conflict and semantic fit separate.\nInput: {\"question\": \"In which city did Conry practice law?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 53, \"text\": \"admitted to the bar and commenced practice in Boston.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 54, \"end\": 174, \"text\": \"He served as president of the Boston Common Council in 1896 and 1897, and was chairman of the board of aldermen in 1898.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 175, \"end\": 274, \"text\": \"Conry was elected as a Democrat to the 57th United States Congress (March 4, 1901 – March 3, 1903).\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 275, \"end\": 420, \"text\": \"He was an unsuccessful candidate for reelection in 1902 to the 58th United States Congress, and resumed the practice of his profession in Boston.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 421, \"end\": 529, \"text\": \"In 1908 Conry was an unsuccessful candidate for the Democratic congressional nomination in the 9th district.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d00\", \"start\": 530, \"end\": 580, \"text\": \"Conry first lost in the Democratic primary, and in\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 60, \"text\": \"was born in Brookline, Massachusetts, on September 12, 1868.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0038-3e135d6719f7:d01\", \"start\": 61, \"end\": 170, \"text\": \"He attended the common schools, studied law, was admitted to the bar and commenced practice in New York City.\"}, \"D